# CHANGELOG.md is append-at-the-top by every PR, so two PRs that both add an
# entry under the same `### Changes` heading conflict on the identical anchor —
# not because they disagree, but because git cannot know both bullets are wanted.
# That conflict fired on essentially every merge once more than one PR was open.
#
# `union` is git's built-in merge driver for exactly this shape: when both sides
# add lines at the same place, it keeps BOTH instead of raising a conflict. It is
# the standard treatment for changelog/authors-style append-only files.
#
# Scope is deliberately this one file. Union is only safe where every line stands
# alone; applying it to code would silently splice two edits into nonsense.
#
# Its one failure mode is duplication (both sides adding the same line, or each
# opening its own `## <version> (TBD)` section), so CI checks the result for
# duplicate version headings — see scripts/check-changelog.sh.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
